@format 1
@id preferences.apply
@title Apply preferences
@area Preferences
@entry input
@summary Collect the options draft, normalize and persist it, apply live settings, and notify when a language change requires restart.
@flow TB
@tag preferences
@tag settings

@alias options = Cadroue.UIShell.PSOptions
@alias preference = Cadroue.UIShell.LPreference
@alias prefStore = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LPreferenceStateStore
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow

[input] User chooses Apply or OK <input>
- Receive the options-window apply command @ options.PSOptionsApply(...)
> collect

[collect] Build preference state <process>
- Copy general, system, playback, timeline, and work controls into the draft @ options.PSOptionsApply(...)
- Normalize values and clone the draft @ options.PSOptionsApply(...)
> persist

[persist] Commit preferences <storage>
- Record differences from the previous preference state @ preference.LPreferenceStateSet(...)
- Replace current preferences and save JSON to application data @ preference.LPreferenceStateSet(...)
- Reapply depot and sidecar roots through the registered callback @ preference.LPreferenceStateSet(...)
> live

[live] Apply live window state <process>
- Apply window, timeline, palette, and volume settings @ window.PWindowOptionsHandle(...)
> language

[language] Check language change <decision>
? "Language changed" > restart-note
? "Language unchanged" > result

[restart-note] Present restart notice <output>
- Tell the user that the new language is applied after restart @ options.PSOptionsApply(...)
= All other preferences are already active and persisted.

[result] Preferences applied <output>
= Preferences are active and persisted.
